% Synthetic proposals for the Arkansas homeowners guidelines
% (arkansas.le): at least one that passes, one that fails for each kind
% of ineligibility the program reads, one per referral, and borderline cases
% (a fact left out, two facts that disagree, a judgment nobody has made yet).
% Each scenario's comment says what it tests. The proposals are invented:
% they test that the guidelines were captured faithfully, not how the
% insurer decides.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the underwriting guidelines it
% cites, it is not an underwriting decision of any insurer, and it is not
% legal or insurance advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them
% for a real application; consult the insurer and a licensed agent. Its
% authors accept no liability for any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base arkansas cases includes these resources:
    arkansas.

the knowledge base arkansas cases includes:

query decision is:
    the decision on which proposal is which action.

query ineligible is:
    which proposal is ineligible under which guideline.

query referred is:
    which proposal must be referred to underwriting under which guideline.

query conditions is:
    which proposal requires a deductible of which amount under which guideline.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        application 101 is eligible.

% A brick-veneer house with a composition roof, central heating and 200 amps;
% the applicant is an AAA member with an Auto Club car policy. Nothing in the
% rule stops it.
scenario clean is:
    application 101 is for the Oak Street house.
    application 101 is dated 2026-09-01.
    the policy form of application 101 is homeowners.
    the applicant of application 101 has a valid AAA membership, according to the applicant.
    the applicant of application 101 has an automobile policy with an Auto Club affiliate, according to the applicant.
    the construction of the Oak Street house is brick veneer, according to the applicant.
    the roof of the Oak Street house is made of composition shingle, according to the applicant.
    the primary heat source of the Oak Street house is central heating, according to the applicant.
    the electrical service of the Oak Street house is 200 amps, according to the applicant.
    the occupancy of the Oak Street house is owner occupied, according to the applicant.
    decision expects answers ["the decision on application 101 is accept"].
    ineligible expects answers [].
    referred expects answers [].

