% A view (docs/user/reference/language.md §17.10): the underwriter's screen
% for a proposal - the application's facts by group, who states each, the
% judgments apart, the decision and the guidelines behind it, what is
% missing, the smallest change that would make the proposal eligible, the
% list of proposals with their decisions, and a draft of the letter.
% (/executive?program=regulatory/underwriting/arkansas_cases&view=underwriting desk)
the view underwriting desk is:
    the title is "Homeowners underwriting desk - Arkansas Rule 05.2".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the application" are
        a proposal is for a dwelling,
        the policy form of a proposal is a form,
        a proposal is dated a date,
        the applicant of a proposal has a valid AAA membership,
        the applicant of a proposal has an automobile policy with an Auto Club affiliate,
        the applicant of a proposal owns no automobile,
        the applicant of a proposal had a claim on a date,
        the cause of a claim is a cause,
        the damage of a claim has been repaired.
    the facts about "the dwelling" are
        the construction of a dwelling is a construction,
        the roof of a dwelling is made of a material,
        the primary heat source of a dwelling is a source,
        the electrical service of a dwelling is a number amps,
        the occupancy of a dwelling is an occupancy,
        a dwelling has knob and tube wiring,
        the premises of a dwelling include a hazard,
        a dwelling is adjacent to a business,
        the inspection report on a dwelling notes a concern.
    the facts about "the household" are
        the household of a proposal keeps an animal,
        the species of an animal is a species.
    the judgments are
        the finding a finding about a thing is an outcome.
    every fact shows who states it.
    the result is the answer to query decision, headed by the action.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the documents of the case are shown beside the facts.
    the result asks what is missing.
    the result can be flipped.
    the cases are listed with their results.
    the draft reads "Application: {the case}.\nDecision: {the result}.\n\nThe guidelines applied:\n{the citations}\n\nThe facts relied on:\n{the facts}".
